// Unique creatures (GDD, section 5): the bosses, which don't exist as summons. Every other enemy of
// the stages and Dungeons is a summon of Data/summons with buffed stats (Core/Battle/BattleFactory.cs).
// Each enemy's element is chosen in the stage (Data/stages.json).
// "stats" are the stats at 6★ level 40 that Data/stat_model.json gives to the boss's "rarity" (natural
// stars) and "role", with no bias. Don't edit them by hand: docs/summon_family_builder.html rewrites
// them ("Recalcular todas"), and the game checks them against the model.
// "healthScale", "attackScale" and "defenseScale" multiply HP, Attack and Defense: enemies have no runes or
// enhancements, and bosses get more HP.
// "minion": true is a unique creature that escorts a boss (the Golem's pillars): it fights at its side, normal
// size, and isn't a boss itself.
// The Dungeon bosses are specialization content (GDD, section 11): each one has a mechanic that a generic
// team can't overpower, and floor 5 is only consistent for a team built and invested for that boss.
// - runic_golem: huge HP and Defense; the Bastion buffs it (Defense+, shield) and enrages it when it falls,
//   the Warden breaks the team's Defense and Attack. Defense Break, buff stealing and timing beat it.
//   The Fire Dwarf Miner is its key: it strips the buffs, ignores and breaks Defense and blocks the healing.
// - elder_wyvern: every enemy afflicts, and its skills hit harder for each debuff on the team (BonusPerStatus).
// - bone_king: "Undying" passive: while it's on the field nobody (ally or foe) gains or loses Impeto, a shield
//   after every action and it always comes back, unless Oblivion silences the passive.
// - drowned_guardian: its wave starts with Counter on every enemy, and its skills keep it up: AoE damage and
//   many attacks get punished. Stun (stunned units don't counter), Blind, Attack Down, stealing the buff and
//   strong single hits beat it; Oblivion doesn't help.
// - celestial_*: the Star Exploration guardians (Data/exploration.json) that no summon family fits; the
//   constellation's influence is the mechanic, their own kit follows the theme.
